<!-- English samajhne ka tarika (tech interviews me)

    Keywords pakdo:
    Har question me kuchh technical keywords hote hain jaise "function", "delay", "print", "every 2 seconds", "multiplication table".
    Tum poora sentence samjho ya na samjho, par keywords pakad lo.

    Break into small parts:
    Example:

    "Write a function that takes a number and prints its multiplication table from 1 to 10 with a delay of 2 seconds between each print."

    Isme parts hain:

    Write a function ✅
    Takes a number ✅
    Prints multiplication table 1 to 10 ✅
    Delay 2 seconds between each print ✅

Mind me Hindi me translate karo:
"Ek function banao jo number lega aur uski table 1 se 10 tak print kare, har print ke beech 2 second ka gap ho."

2️⃣ Problem ko solve karne ka thinking process
Chahe English clear ho ya nahi, tum yeh fixed approach follow karo:

Step 1: Inputs and Outputs identify karo
    Input: number (e.g., 2)
    Output: 1 se 10 tak table print ho

Step 2: Requirements samjho
    Normal table print ✅
    Delay add karna ✅

Step 3: Code ke liye building blocks identify karo
    Loop (for or while) table banane ke liye
    Delay ke liye setTimeout ya setInterval
    Condition table stop karne ke liye

Step 4: Pehle simple version banao
    Pehle without delay table print karo
    Fir delay add karo step-by-step

3️⃣ Interview me jab kuchh samajh na aaye
Clarify karo:
    "Could you please repeat the question slowly?"
    "Do you mean printing the table all at once or line by line?"
    (Interviewer samjhega ki tum clear understanding chahte ho, ye positive hota hai.)

Example pucho:
    "Can you give me an example output for the input 2?"
    (Example milte hi tumhe instantly samajh aa jayega.)

4️⃣ Practice habit banao
    Tum English + coding dono improve karne ke liye yeh karo:
    LeetCode Easy + GeeksForGeeks problems solve karo
    Har problem ka statement English me padho, Hindi me translate karo, fir solve karo
    Timer lagao (5–10 min thinking, fir coding)
    Code likhne ke baad explain karo (English me bol kar) -->